From 79e476dc6e181d6c1034e50f1f2f0ad677d59959 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 19:17:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08124/11362] [outer-loop] Settle GENERATION vs SELECTION: the
 induce gate is not discarding usable world models

Scores 250 distinct saved engine bodies (4 corpora, 23 games) on transitions they
were never fitted to, against the ACTUAL shipped gate quantities at their ACTUAL
thresholds. Pre-registered as a census: no treatment, no pairing, no p-value --
the pre-stated inferential device is the rule of three.

ANSWER: GENERATION. And tn36 shows it is about the GAMES, not the method -- the
generator writes a PERFECT world model there reproducibly (6 of 8 best-of-N
candidates at change_accuracy 1.0000, precision 1.0000, on BOTH a row-by-row
proven 17-row held-out split AND 120 independently collected transitions).
Across 3 splits, 4 corpora and 23 games, engines clearing the de-inflated
change_accuracy>=0.5 come from that ONE game.

- gate-faithful split: hidden-state trust gate cleared by 0 of 250 (max 0.4843
  vs 0.5; 95% upper bound on the clear-rate 0.0119)
- the SELECTION case, stated at its strongest then tested: 61 of 250 clear
  cell_recall>=0.5 over 13 games, 15 at precision>=0.9 -- and 0 of those 15
  survive on 120 fresh rows, where on 4 of their 5 games a MEASURED stateless
  ceiling of 1.0 rules out distribution shift as the excuse
- the actual live rejection set is lower still: 0 of 22 hidden-state and 0 of 28
  plain attempts reach 0.5; 16 of 22 fail nondegeneracy at ANY threshold
- exp6018's "held-out exact accuracy uniformly 0.0" REPRODUCED in substance with
  the CURRENT generator and an explicit non-empty split, so neither of its two
  self-named confounds explains it -- but REFINED: raw exact accuracy is not
  uniformly zero, it is no-op inflated

Separately and NOT the bottleneck: the exact-match gate is genuinely
mis-specified -- it scores a 0.9615-recall/1.0-precision engine identically to
`return grid`. Relaxing it is still not the lever: the relaxed metric already
shipped as a flag, already ran as a live arm with 0 plans, and the engines that
clear it do not generalise.

Four self-corrections recorded rather than quietly applied: the oracle control
caught itself (last-write-wins is not the stateless ceiling; replaced with the
modal predictor), change_gate_decision returns passed=True/gate_disabled when
off and was first read as a result, byte-identical engine bodies were first
counted as independent observations, and an acceptance gate first asserted that
no unparseable engine EXISTS rather than that it is excluded -- 7 of 48
best-of-N candidates are not valid Python, which is itself a generation-side
result and is now reported.

No default flipped, no episode played, no game scored or online. Evidence dirs
read-only; every worker points CARNOT_ARC_E3_DIR at scratch before import.

